# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.firecrawl/

# Model weights and caches — never commit, these are 1-31 GB each
# .cache/ is the repo-local cache root (see src/stt/paths.py); it holds tens of
# gigabytes of downloaded weights.
.cache/
models/
*.pt
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.mlmodelc/

# Audio and transcripts
data/audio/**
!data/audio/.gitkeep
# Hand-corrected reference transcripts ARE tracked -- they are the only
# ground truth we have for audio the models cannot have trained on, and
# unlike the FLEURS sets they cannot be re-fetched.
!data/reference/**
# FLEURS audio is re-fetchable, but its reference transcripts and corpus
# identity are the other half of every published CER -- without them a
# clone can audit nothing. `/**` rather than the bare directory because a
# negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
data/fleurs*/**
!data/fleurs*/references.tsv
!data/fleurs*/corpus.json
# Resampled 16 kHz mono copies produced by stt.audio, and ad-hoc slices
data/.converted/
data/.slices/
outputs/**
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/README.md
# The runs behind every number in docs/findings.md. 1.3 MB, and the only way to
# audit a published figure without re-running 88 GB of models for hours --
# which is the same reason data/reference/ is tracked. Scratch runs stay out.
!outputs/t120-*.jsonl
!outputs/evidence-fleurs-test-mms.jsonl
!outputs/evidence-fleurs-test-dolphin.jsonl
!outputs/evidence-fleurs-dev-seamless.jsonl
# ...except a vote or route artifact, which `stt vote` and `stt route` write
# with trusted=False and no model provenance by construction. Such a file can
# never back a published number; the evidence renderer recomputes the vote from
# its constituent runs instead, so tracking one would only invite it to be cited.
outputs/t120-voted.jsonl
# The held-out eternity-*.jsonl runs stay out: they are complete transcripts of
# copyrighted third-party audio, and the audio itself is deliberately not in the
# repo either (see data/reference/README.md). They cannot back a published
# number today in any case -- their reference join is broken and they carry no
# canonical audio_id -- so nothing is lost by keeping them local.

# A hand-authored architecture page nothing links to. Deliberately not adopted:
# CLAUDE.md is the one home for that description, and a second unlinked copy no
# guard covers would drift out of agreement with it. Kept on disk, out of git.
docs/architecture.html

# Third-party sources built from scratch
vendor/

# Secrets (ElevenLabs / Google Cloud keys, for later backends)
.env
*.json.key
service-account*.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
